00:42:05.656 --> 00:42:07.725 align:start size:84% position:16%
for all the reasons
you've just described.

00:42:07.725 --> 00:42:09.360
I don't think it
can be repaired.

00:42:09.360 --> 00:42:11.495
I can tell you, and I think
I've been in California,

00:42:11.495 --> 00:42:13.998 align:start size:84% position:16%
my guys at the counter
91 days right now

00:42:13.998 --> 00:42:15.132
I've been in Florida.

00:42:15.132 --> 00:42:17.201
And since I left,

00:42:17.201 --> 00:42:19.136
I feel like I live in
a different country.

00:42:19.136 --> 00:42:22.106 align:start size:88% position:13%
And the problem is that
in the free states,

00:42:22.106 --> 00:42:23.207
they're not gonna want anything.

00:42:23.207 --> 00:42:24.775
Nobody in Florida wants anything

00:42:24.775 --> 00:42:26.176
from the people in California.

00:42:26.176 --> 00:42:28.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the people in
California want something

00:42:28.112 --> 00:42:29.513
from the people in Florida,

00:42:29.513 --> 00:42:31.882
that's an untenable position.

00:42:31.882 --> 00:42:33.884
- You know, the government,

00:42:33.884 --> 00:42:35.419 align:start size:84% position:16%
the federal government
fears two things.

00:42:35.419 --> 00:42:39.757
It fears loss of power over
certain geographical areas.

00:42:39.757 --> 00:42:41.759
So if Florida succeeds,

00:42:41.759 --> 00:42:44.361 align:start size:84% position:16%
feds couldn't control
Florida at all.

00:42:44.361 --> 00:42:47.264
And it fears loss
of tax dollars.

00:42:48.699 --> 00:42:50.701
If everybody who
lives in Florida

00:42:50.701 --> 00:42:53.103
didn't have to pay a
federal income tax,

00:42:53.103 --> 00:42:54.672 align:start size:84% position:16%
the feds would be
pulling their hair out

00:42:54.672 --> 00:42:56.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
because of the same thing
would happen in Texas

00:42:56.674 --> 00:42:59.843
and Montana and other states.

00:42:59.843 --> 00:43:02.813
And this behemoth
that we've allowed

00:43:02.813 --> 00:43:06.016
to grow from Woodrow
Wilson to Joe Biden

00:43:06.016 --> 00:43:09.386 align:start size:88% position:13%
and Republicans are just
as bad, just as bad.

00:43:09.386 --> 00:43:12.256
You know, George Bush
borrowed 3 trillion,

00:43:12.256 --> 00:43:14.358 align:start size:84% position:16%
Donald Trump
borrowed 2 trillion,

00:43:14.358 --> 00:43:17.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
Joe Biden borrowed 1
trillion in just one year.

00:43:17.995 --> 00:43:22.933
That we've allowed
this monstrosity to
get out of control,

00:43:22.933 --> 00:43:27.638
to mortgage the future
to sap our liberties,

00:43:27.638 --> 00:43:32.643
the only way around it would
be to let it go by the wayside.

00:43:34.211 --> 00:43:35.412
- Well then I have to ask you,

00:43:35.412 --> 00:43:37.481
what keeps you in the northeast?

00:43:37.481 --> 00:43:39.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
What's keeping you in
Jersey with the high taxes

00:43:39.683 --> 00:43:41.118
and everything else?

00:43:41.118 --> 00:43:42.386 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean this is where the
rubber meets the road, right?

00:43:42.386 --> 00:43:43.554
- I love my farm, I
love this property.

00:43:43.554 --> 00:43:45.489
I love the real estate.

00:43:45.489 --> 00:43:47.091
You are not the only friend

00:43:47.091 --> 00:43:51.395 align:start size:84% position:16%
that asks me that
almost all of them do,

00:43:51.395 --> 00:43:54.064
but you are one of the
happiest people I know.

00:43:55.466 --> 00:43:56.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
- I'm telling you man
that I'm a lot happier now

00:43:56.433 --> 00:43:58.435
than I was two months ago.

00:43:58.435 --> 00:44:01.772
- You know, Fox sent me
to California for a year

00:44:01.772 --> 00:44:03.173
to do a reality show.

00:44:03.173 --> 00:44:04.341
I played myself.

00:44:04.341 --> 00:44:05.743 align:start size:84% position:16%
It was called
"Power of Attorney."

00:44:05.743 --> 00:44:07.077
It was a "Judge Judy" like show.

00:44:07.077 --> 00:44:08.379
We had celebrity lawyers.

00:44:08.379 --> 00:44:10.714
So the OJ case had just ended.

00:44:10.714 --> 00:44:12.383
We had all the lawyers from OJ,

00:44:12.383 --> 00:44:15.219
the late great F. Lee Bailey
and I became great friends

00:44:15.219 --> 00:44:17.021
from this show.

00:44:17.021 --> 00:44:20.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
There were half hour
shows, superstar lawyers.

00:44:20.391 --> 00:44:23.494 align:start size:97% position:3%
The typical case was the
dry cleaner ruined my dress,

00:44:23.494 --> 00:44:25.696
but he also tried to
pick up my sister.

00:44:25.696 --> 00:44:27.965
It was nonsense like that.

00:44:27.965 --> 00:44:29.466
I hated it.

00:44:29.466 --> 00:44:32.603
I hated all that
time in California.

00:44:32.603 --> 00:44:34.938
I couldn't wait to come home.

00:44:34.938 --> 00:44:36.407
- And that's while
it was still open.

00:44:36.407 --> 00:44:38.108
I mean, geez, okay.

00:44:38.108 --> 00:44:40.377 align:start size:84% position:16%
I wanna cover one
more big one for you,

00:44:40.377 --> 00:44:42.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
which I'm covering pretty
much every day here.

00:44:42.046 --> 00:44:43.380 align:start size:84% position:16%
And it frames almost
everything I do,

00:44:43.380 --> 00:44:45.149
which is some of
the big tech stuff

00:44:45.149 --> 00:44:47.518
and where the law
should be involved

00:44:47.518 --> 00:44:48.952
and where it should not,

00:44:48.952 --> 00:44:51.422 align:start size:84% position:16%
and how that relates
to free speech.

00:44:51.422 --> 00:44:54.525 align:start size:97% position:3%
Do you view these platforms,
Facebook, Twitter,

00:44:54.525 --> 00:44:57.728
et cetera, as sort of
the new public square.

00:44:57.728 --> 00:45:00.531
And if they squelch
a person or a story,

00:45:00.531 --> 00:45:02.166
obviously in the last week,

00:45:02.166 --> 00:45:05.836
we now know that the Hunter
Biden laptop story is legit.

00:45:05.836 --> 00:45:07.738
And yet Facebook and Twitter,

00:45:07.738 --> 00:45:10.340 align:start size:88% position:13%
not only banned the
story from being posted,

00:45:10.340 --> 00:45:13.644
but literally down the New
York Post's Twitter account.

00:45:14.812 --> 00:45:16.947 align:start size:84% position:16%
Are there some
legal remedies here

00:45:16.947 --> 00:45:19.016
or is this just left to
congressional hearings

00:45:19.016 --> 00:45:21.185 align:start size:88% position:13%
that nothing ever
happened for the reasons

00:45:21.185 --> 00:45:22.986
that you've been laying
out this whole time?

00:45:22.986 --> 00:45:26.423
- In my opinion, it should
be left to the free market.

00:45:26.423 --> 00:45:29.493
Facebook in my view
is just a glorified

00:45:29.493 --> 00:45:30.961
high tech bulletin board.

00:45:30.961 --> 00:45:32.429
They own the bulletin board

00:45:32.429 --> 00:45:34.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
and if they don't like
something that was posted,

00:45:34.264 --> 00:45:35.299
they can take it down.

00:45:35.299 --> 00:45:36.233
I don't like it.

00:45:36.233 --> 00:45:38.502
I've been criticized by them,

00:45:38.502 --> 00:45:40.370
but they are a private entity.

00:45:40.370 --> 00:45:41.772
The last thing in
the world we want

00:45:41.772 --> 00:45:44.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
is the federal government
involved in speech

00:45:44.608 --> 00:45:46.810
because the government
will favor the speech

00:45:46.810 --> 00:45:48.512
of its benefactors.

00:45:48.512 --> 00:45:50.547
And it will favor
the speech it likes

00:45:50.547 --> 00:45:53.650
and disfavor the speech
that is critical of it.

00:45:53.650 --> 00:45:55.419
The free market in ideas,

00:45:55.419 --> 00:45:59.323
as well as the free market in
electronic bulletin boards,

00:45:59.323 --> 00:46:01.759
if you'll pardon that phrase,

00:46:01.759 --> 00:46:03.127
is what should resolve this.

00:46:03.127 --> 00:46:05.429
So someone like Charles Koch

00:46:05.429 --> 00:46:07.931
should start his own Facebook

00:46:07.931 --> 00:46:10.901
and you'll watch Mark
Zuckerberg's profits

00:46:10.901 --> 00:46:14.138
go way down as hundreds
of millions of people

00:46:14.138 --> 00:46:18.142 align:start size:88% position:13%
migrate over to
another bulletin board.

00:46:18.142 --> 00:46:20.944 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Hint, hint, I suppose
at Charles Koch.

00:46:20.944 --> 00:46:21.779
- Hint, hint.

00:46:21.779 --> 00:46:22.713
I know him well,

00:46:22.713 --> 00:46:24.848
and he's turned down this idea,

00:46:24.848 --> 00:46:25.949
but I keep pushing it.

00:46:28.285 --> 00:46:29.887 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Judge, I've
thoroughly enjoyed this.

00:46:29.887 --> 00:46:34.291
I hope you'll come back and
good luck in Jersey man.

00:46:34.291 --> 00:46:36.894 align:start size:84% position:16%
Listen if the
country does split,

00:46:36.894 --> 00:46:38.662
I've got a guest room.

00:46:38.662 --> 00:46:40.264
- You're very kind.

00:46:40.264 --> 00:46:41.665 align:start size:81% position:19%
It's a pleasure
to be on with you,

00:46:41.665 --> 00:46:43.333
I've admired your work for years

00:46:43.333 --> 00:46:44.468
and I'd love to do it again.

00:46:44.468 --> 00:46:45.903
Thank you, Dave.

00:46:45.903 --> 00:46:47.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
Maybe you'll come on
"Judging Freedom" with me.

00:46:47.137 --> 00:46:48.605
- I think I'm coming
on in a couple weeks.

00:46:48.605 --> 00:46:49.840
That's what they're telling me.

00:46:49.840 --> 00:46:50.874
- I think so.

00:46:50.874 --> 00:46:52.342
- Great.

